</td><td valign="top" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;page-break-after:auto;"><p style="text-align: left;page-break-after:auto" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_f7e9a3fb-91ee-83ff-976c-ec87e8b8e631" id="_f7e9a3fb-91ee-83ff-976c-ec87e8b8e631"></a><b>Mandatory in S-102</b><br/> A single value may be provided when all axes have a common resolution.<br/> For multiple value provision, use axis order as specified in dataset.<br/> May be approximate for ungeorectified data (<b>not applicable to this edition of S-102</b>).<br/> For example, for 5-metre resolution, the value 5 must be encoded.<br/> See  <a href="#s100-dataCoverage-params-note1">Note</a>.</p>
</td></tr></tbody><tfoot><tr><td colspan="6" style="border-top:0pt;mso-border-top-alt:0pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;"><div class="Note"><a name="s100-dataCoverage-params-note1" id="s100-dataCoverage-params-note1"></a><p class="Note"><span class="note_label">NOTE<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span></span>If the grid cell size varies over the extent of the grid, an approximated value based on model parameters or production metadata should be used.</p></div></td></tr></tfoot></table></div>


</div>

